/-
  boatsched — Tier-2 verification library.

  This library contains the **Aeneas-extracted model of the real Rust domain
  core** (`rust/crates/core`: `validate`, `ProblemConfig`, and the pure authz
  predicates) together with the **refinement proofs** that bind that model to
  the hand-written spec in `BoatschedSpec`.

  Layers:
  * `BoatschedExtract.Types`, `.Funs`   — generated by Charon+Aeneas (do not edit).
  * `BoatschedExtract.FunsExternal`      — hand-filled models of the std-library
                                           primitives Aeneas leaves opaque.
  * `BoatschedExtract.Refinement`        — the `EXT-*` theorems: the extracted
                                           Rust functions refine `BoatschedSpec`,
                                           for all inputs and panic-free.

  Regenerate the model with (see spec/README.md for the pinned toolchain):
      charon cargo --preset=aeneas --start-from 'boatsched_core::validate' \
        --start-from 'boatsched_core::authz::can_perform' \
        --start-from 'boatsched_core::authz::guard_set_admin'
      aeneas -backend lean -split-files -loops-to-rec -subdir BoatschedExtract -dest <spec> boatsched_core.llbc
-/
import BoatschedExtract.Types
import BoatschedExtract.Funs
import BoatschedExtract.FunsExternal
import BoatschedExtract.Refinement
